  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The FY2026 to date list of top government contractors shows concentration in a few large companies and suppliers. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO leads the ranking with $13.4B in contract obligations. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. follows with $13.1B, and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP holds $12.6B. The Department of Defense and civilian agencies obligated a combined total of $207B during the fiscal year to date. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice in the top entries with $10.2B and $9.7B of obligations, reflecting multiple large awardees or subsidiary reporting. Other major contractors include MCKESSON CORPORATION with $9.9B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION with $8.6B, RAYTHEON COMPANY with $6.3B, BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED with $5.9B, and THE BOEING COMPANY with $5.9B. These figures are contract obligations recorded for the fiscal year to date, so current-year totals are partial and will change as the fiscal year progresses. This ranking highlights the largest single-company obligation totals reported so far in FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top five contractors by obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is the top contractor with $13.4B in obligations. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is second with $13.1B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is third with $12.6B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears with $10.2B as the fourth-largest obligation."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How big is the market represented by these obligations so far in FY2026?",
        "body": "The reported total obligations for the fiscal year to date equal $207B. Several large contractors together account for substantial shares of that total, including names with single-company obligations above $5.9B. Current-year totals are partial, so the $207B figure reflects obligations recorded to date rather than a full fiscal year sum."
      }
    ]
  },
